{"id":"a03035be819b8e1f","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-collapse-forcing.md","title":"Levy Collapse","display":"thm-collapse-forcing — Levy Collapse","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-collapse-forcing","aliases":["58-thm-collapse-forcing","Levy Collapse","Collapse Forcing","Levy Collapse Theorem"],"display":"thm-collapse-forcing — Levy Collapse","depends_on":["[[58-df-collapse]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md]]","[[../batch07/58-df-name.md]]","[[../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-ctm.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-collapse-forcing"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-collapse-forcing</span><span>Levy Collapse</span><span>Collapse Forcing</span><span>Levy Collapse Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-collapse-forcing — Levy Collapse"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"db7c5834b8f0957b\" href=\"?note=db7c5834b8f0957b\" title=\"58-df-collapse\">58-df-collapse</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"06ee5d7ff126e916\" href=\"?note=06ee5d7ff126e916\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md\">../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-name.md\">../batch07/58-df-name.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"46b2495f214783c3\" href=\"?note=46b2495f214783c3\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md\">../batch14/58-df-forcing-relation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-ctm.md\">../batch06/58-df-ctm.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,P,R,\\lambda,\\kappa,\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}}\\in V\">\\(M,P,R,\\lambda,\\kappa,\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}}\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\\)</span> is the imported countable-transitive-model predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S\\)</span> are the imported cardinal predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P=\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)\">\\(P=\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R=\\leq_{\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)}\">\\(R=\\leq_{\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)}\\)</span> are the canonical Levy-collapse carrier and order</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span> are the imported name and fully parameterized forcing predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}}(v_0,v_1)\">\\(\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}}(v_0,v_1)\\)</span> is the object-language formula code saying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v_1=v_0^+\">\\(v_1=v_0^+\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}collapse\\text{-}forcing}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land\\lambda,\\kappa,\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\lambda)\n\\land\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\kappa)\n\\land\\lambda&lt;\\kappa\n\\land P=\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)\n\\land R=\\leq_{\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)}\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check\\lambda,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check\\kappa,P)\n\\to\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S(\nM,\\varnothing,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}},\n\\langle\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa\\rangle,P,R).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}collapse\\text{-}forcing}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZFC})\n\\land\\lambda,\\kappa,\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa\\in M\n\\land\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\lambda)\n\\land\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\kappa)\n\\land\\lambda&lt;\\kappa\n\\land P=\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)\n\\land R=\\leq_{\\operatorname{Coll}(\\lambda,{&lt;}\\kappa)}\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check\\lambda,P)\n\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\check\\kappa,P)\n\\to\\mathrm{ZfcForcingRelation}_S(\nM,\\varnothing,\\varphi_{\\mathrm{succ}},\n\\langle\\check\\lambda,\\check\\kappa\\rangle,P,R).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Levy (1960s): developed collapse forcing.</li>\n<li>Key: collapses range <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> simultaneously.</li>\n<li>With the standard presentation it is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"&lt;\\lambda\">\\(&lt;\\lambda\\)</span>-closed and, under the\ninaccessible hypothesis on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>, has the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-chain condition.</li>\n<li>It preserves cardinals at most <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> and collapses the ground-model\ncardinals strictly between <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>; it does not preserve all\ncardinals below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Applications: create models where <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa = \\lambda^+\">\\(\\kappa = \\lambda^+\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Used in: consistency of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa = \\omega_2\">\\(\\kappa = \\omega_2\\)</span>, singular cardinal constructions.</li>\n<li>Solovay model: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Col}(\\omega, &lt;\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{Col}(\\omega, &lt;\\kappa)\\)</span> for inaccessible <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> gives all sets measurable.</li>\n<li>Levy collapse + other forcing: complex model constructions.</li>\n<li>The extension-level prose has been replaced by the exact six-argument forcing statement: ground model, top condition, formula code, name tuple, carrier, and order are all explicit.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-collapse","status":"resolved","id":"db7c5834b8f0957b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-collapse]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc198002